  "Where the calendar bug turns into data loss: the sequence is consistent — the date breaks → the user tries delete-and-reinstall as a workaround → the history is gone because there is no backup — 'I tried restarting the app and my phone, and even deleted/redownloaded it and reentered all my habits. No luck' (2★); 'I tried deleting it and adding habits again but still stuck on 1/30… Update- waited til the next day and app was back to normal just sad I lost my data from uninstalling it' (5★); 'I just wish I didn't have to delete and reinstalled it every 30 days for the calendar to work' (4★); 'When I manually moved it to July, it did not keep track of my habits and I would've had to re-enter them all again' (3★); the most actionable inference in the report: the app's own reviews taught users that reinstalling fixes the date, reinstalling destroys their data, and the bug fix alone does not close this loop — an export or backup path does, and three independent reviewers requested one",
